\viewkind4\uc1\pard\sa160\sl252\slmult1\i\f0\fs22 Waste Management Recycling Education Representative Bobby Bell announced the \ldblquote Free Paper Shredding\rdblquote  event at Mira Costa High School on Saturday, April 25, 2026, from 9:00 AM - 11:00 AM; and the \ldblquote Backyard & Worm Composting Class\rdblquote  at the Manhattan Beach Botanical Garden at Polliwog Park on Saturday, May 2, 2026, at 10:00 AM.\cf1\b\i0\line\line\cf0\b0\i Library Manager Cassandra Sargent announced the \ldblquote Rhythms and Roots\rdblquote  program with Louie Cruz Beltran on Wednesday, April 29, 2026, from 3:30 PM to 4:30 PM.\cf1\b\i0\line\line\cf0\b0\i Environmental Programs Administrator Britny Coker-Moen thanked the community for attending the Tree Planting Event that occurred last weekend. She also announced a \ldblquote Bioblitz by the Dunes\rdblquote  event, in collaboration with the Bay Foundation and other organizations, at Rosecrans Avenue and The Strand on Saturday, April 25, 2026, from 10:00 AM to 12:00 PM. In addition, she shared that the City is offering a full month of activities for the community and that participants may pick up a stamp card at City Hall to track completed activities for a chance to earn a prize.\line\line Financial Services Manager Emy-Rose Hanna announced the \ldblquote Business License Tax Forum,\rdblquote  at the City Council Chambers and Zoom on Thursday, April 23, 2026, at 12:00 PM.\line\line\pard Mayor Lesser invited the community to attend his final \ldblquote Coffee with the Mayor\rdblquote  at Metlox Plaza on Friday, May 1, 2026, from 9:00 AM to 10:00 AM.\cf2\i0\f1\fs24\par
